# Privacy Policy — Kuido

_Last updated: November 21, 2026_

Kuido is your pet's health and care record: it keeps vaccines, dewormer, flea and tick,
medications, grooming, vet visits, weight and documents, and reminds you of what's due. It was made
to work with no account and no server: **what you enter stays on your phone**. This policy explains
what the app uses, why, and what happens on the basic plan, which shows ads. It is the full version
of the summary the app shows in Settings › About and terms of use › Privacy policy.

## 1. What stays on your phone

Your pets, care, records, weigh-ins, photos, PDFs, contacts (vet, clinic, groomer), your ID card
details and your settings are stored only on the device. Reminders are scheduled on the phone itself.
We have no server, create no account and never receive a copy of this data.

The contacts you add are other people's data: they stay on the phone and only leave it if you
include them in a backup, a spreadsheet or a pet file.

## 2. Permissions

Each permission is requested only when you use the feature, and the app keeps working if you say no.
Kuido never asks for location, the device's contacts or the calendar.

| Permission | What for |
|---|---|
| Notifications | Remind you of each care at the time you choose. |
| Exact alarm (Android) | Only for medications with a set time, so the reminder arrives on time; requested with an explanation at the first such medication. Without it, the reminder arrives at about that time. |
| Camera | Take a photo of your pet, a vaccine label or a document, when you tap to take it. |
| Photos | Pick photos with the system photo picker: the app only sees the photos you pick. Saving the pet ID card to Photos only adds the image. |
| Files | Save and open the backups, spreadsheets, PDFs and pet files you choose and, with Premium, the folder you pick for automatic backup copies. |

## 3. Backups, files and sharing

Something only leaves the device when you send it: a backup (`.zip`), the spreadsheet, a pet file
(`.kuido`), the health record as a PDF or image, the pet ID card or an email to support. You choose
where it goes (email, cloud, messages, another person); from then on, the policy of that service
applies. The ID card and QR only carry what you turned on; the health record never includes an
address, personal notes or costs.

In an email to support, the device details (model, system, app version and the reminder
diagnostics) are only included if you leave that option on, and the email is sent from your own
email app.

## 4. Ads (basic plan)

The basic plan shows ads from **Google AdMob**. To show and measure ads, Google may collect the
device's advertising ID, the IP address (and the approximate location derived from it), technical
device and system details such as the model and language, and interactions with ads.

- Where the law requires it (such as the European Economic Area, the UK and Switzerland), the app
  asks for your consent first through Google's consent platform, and you can change your choice later.
- On iPhone, the system asks whether the app may track you across apps; without permission, the
  advertising ID is not used. If you decline, ads continue without personalization.
- None of your pets' data goes to the ad network.
- With **Premium** there are no ads and the ads SDK is not started.

How Google uses this data: <https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites>.

## 5. Purchases

Subscriptions and the lifetime purchase are processed by **Google Play** or the **App Store**. We
never receive your payment details; the app only asks the store whether Premium is active.

## 6. Internet

The app uses the internet only for ads (basic plan), the store (purchases and restore purchases) and
the support email you choose to send. Everything else works offline.

## 7. Pet care, not veterinary advice

Kuido organizes your pet's care; it is not a human or veterinary health service. It never suggests
medications, doses or diagnoses, and suggested care is a general starting point. Always follow your
vet's advice.

## 8. Children

The app is not directed to children under 13 and does not knowingly collect children's data.

## 9. Retention and deletion

Data stays on the phone until you delete it. What you move to the Trash stays there for 30 days and
is then deleted for good; you can also delete forever or empty the Trash sooner. **Settings › Backup
& data › Erase all data** takes the app back to the start with no data; uninstalling the app
also deletes everything. Backups and files you exported stay wherever you saved them. Since we keep
none of your data, there is nothing to delete on our side; requests about ad data can be made to
Google in the ad settings of your account or device.

## 10. Your rights

You have the rights provided by the LGPD (Brazil), the GDPR (Europe) and similar laws. Write to us at
the email below with any question or request.

## 11. Changes

If this policy changes, the date at the top is updated and relevant changes are announced in the app.

